<article class="env-lemma" id="0BWG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BWG">Lemma <span data-tag="0BWG">49.12.3</span>.</a> Let $f : Y \to X$ be a morphism of Noetherian schemes. If $f$ satisfies the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0BWE" data-tag="0BWE">49.10.1</a> then the different $\mathfrak {D}_ f$ of $f$ is the Kähler different of $f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemmas <a href="/tag/0BW6" data-tag="0BW6">49.9.3</a> and <a href="/tag/0BWF" data-tag="0BWF">49.10.4</a> the different of $f$ affine locally is the same as the Noether different. Then the lemma follows from the computation of the Noether different and the Kähler different on standard affine pieces done in Lemmas <a href="/tag/0BVZ" data-tag="0BVZ">49.7.4</a> and <a href="/tag/0BWD" data-tag="0BWD">49.12.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>